LittleBigPlanet scrapbooked world of  paper mache cardboard and middle grading  is bigger and brighter in  LittleBigPlanet 3 with more bits and  bobs to occupy your time and tickle  every last one of your fancies it's more  of the same LittleBigPlanet you've come  to know and love and despite a handful  of unfortunate glitches some seriously  sweet new additions like you gadgets and  characters keep the overall whimsy of  the game intact LittleBigPlanet 3 story  is a ground of well trodden tropes but  having the whole thing enacted with  stack people and a sentient light bulb  voiced by Hugh Laurie allows you to wave  those cliches an inventor named Newton  kidnaps a boy and makes off for the  planet Buncombe newton then releases a  trio of ancient evil titans that possess  him and the only way to save him is to  awaken three ancient heroes that first  defeated the Titans surprise surprise  newcomers odd sock toggle and sweet  Donn's  the thing about these new characters is  that while they're fun to play they're  not particularly playable or present  rather each character is confined to the  hub world in which they are unlocked for  example once you unlock odd sock in the  mangle would swap hub you can only use  odd sock in the mangle with swamp levels  the same goes for toggle and swoop but  Sackboy is playable in all worlds and in  some story campaign levels he's  mandatory each hub world also offers  only one point a small doorway at which  to swap characters I'm disappointed that  after months of being tantalized with  the idea of gathering three friends and  playing as all four characters at once  he rarely can as of Little Big Planet 3  is launched for character levels are  severely limited which is maddening and  saddening all at once if you want to  play the whole game as someone other  than sac boy  level structure itself is very basic  within each hub Sackboy has to find  marbles that when placed together will  awaken that hubs hero marbles are  rewarded for finishing main campaign  levels and when you're not marble  hunting you can explore hubs for hidden  side quests and minigames these  minigames range from go-kart building to  lemmings like challenges and that you  have to guide six or more sack boys to a  finish line each quest is introduced by  an NPC that is just as colorful and  strange as a world itself way up in  great rocket space will take that a  special gadget get it you will need some  sort of poke pad  playing multi-planet three alone is  great when your score chasing but  playing with friends is infinitely  better helping each other navigate  sticky traps and collect prize bubbles  is rewarding as it helps the game  transcend from just something on a  screen to something affecting the  real-world space you and your play  partners will shout at each other laugh  and maybe engage in some playful  competition throwing each other into  spikes or dropping them from dizzying  heights the physics are still on the too  floaty side with characters listlessly  drifting through jumps and free Falls  but once you get the hang of how each  character works it feels immensely  satisfying to land a difficult jumping  scene with toggle or complete a speedrun  with odd sock LittleBigPlanet 3 may not  be the most solid of physics based  platformers but it definitely feels good  I can't get over how beautiful this game  looks the world of bunkum is bright and  detailed NPCs are also fully voiced for  the first time in the LittleBigPlanet  series and between the myriad sounds and  sights it's like an adorable Technicolor  acid trip and a beautiful and  untouchable bubble of sunshine but it's  the level creation tools that wrap more  depths and sparkle into LittleBigPlanet  universe unlike anything we've been  given thus far user created content is  the spine of the LittleBigPlanet  franchise and sumo digital has gone to  almost unreasonable heights to provide  not only a seemingly endless well of  tools but attractive ways with which to  learn how to use them the Popat puzzle  section is a goldmine for players who  don't have or want the desire to build  levels because it succeeds in forcing  that desire onto them these puzzles wrap  tutorials for each major element in your  creation arsenal from editing corners to  deleting objects and adding poisonous  things into meaningful mini-games these  minigames yield real rewards like new  sackboy material stickers and other  goodies LittleBigPlanet 3 gives you  every reason to learn to manipulate it  and inspires you to begin manipulating  immediately as someone who is never  really good at making a game content I  was driven to try it simply because I  now knew clearly how to use it and I  stuck with it because I was no longer  blindly groping around trying to  discover how things work LittleBigPlanet  3 is entertaining and sweet but things  get sour if you run into any of its  strange bugs sack boys twitch  uncontrollably or randomly bounce around  the screen out of nowhere or fail to  respawn in certain levels a few times I  spawned behind a moving boss character  in a side-scrolling level which broke  the game and forced me to restart these  bugs can also make you lose progress and  more than once I found myself ready to  give up because I had to begin levels  again over no fault of mine it's  frustrating and taints and otherwise  engaging experience bugs and new  character scarcity aside LittleBigPlanet  3 is an enjoyable game tackling a level  with three or four players offers for  some hilarious mishaps and trials and  teamwork and even playing tool tutorials  online with a buddy has its merits all  in all the game is gorgeous to look at  and offers a genuine challenge more so  than any other franchise title today  a little demonstration  mara Bella's  come now to ziggurat I will explain  everything
 

